<article class="env-lemma" id="0GVH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GVH">Lemma <span data-tag="0GVH">15.130.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $P$ be a projective module. Let $s \in P$. There exists a finite free module $F$ and a finite free direct summand $K \subset F \oplus P$ with $(0, s) \in K$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0GVG" data-tag="0GVG">15.130.2</a> we can find a (possibly infinite) free module $F$ such that $F \oplus P$ is free. Then of course $(0, s)$ is contained in a finite free direct summand $K \subset F \oplus P$. In turn $K$ is contained in $F' \oplus P$ where $F' \subset F$ is a finite free direct summand. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>